==================================================================================
                      route      n=1000     n=4000    n=16000    n=64000    slope      verdict
             theta=0  (BCT)     0.05729    0.02962    0.01448    0.00714   -0.502     vanishes
    theta=1  (spatial sign)     0.02815    0.01458    0.00693    0.00352   -0.504     vanishes
            theta=2  (SSCM)     0.02571    0.01345    0.00629    0.00319   -0.506     vanishes
             CF  e^{i<u,X>}     0.01509    0.00762    0.00370    0.00190   -0.501     vanishes

READ-OFF.
  Cauchy      : NO route vanishes, the bounded ones included.  A bounded
                test function does not repair an error with no mean.
                (MI) is undefined here, so nothing is being violated --
                the manuscript was asserting a hypothesis it had ruled out.
  Pareto-1.5  : every route vanishes (E|eps| < inf gives exactness) but
                the log-slope is well short of -1/2 -- consistency without
                a sqrt(n) CLT, which needs E eps^2.
  Gaussian    : every route vanishes at the -1/2 CLT rate.

  CONCLUSION: the error-side moment requirement is a property of eps, not
  of the feature.  One moment for consistency, two for inference, on every
  route.  The paper must say so; the earlier manuscript said the reverse.

